  "description": "CACFUM crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C27 H36 Cl1 Ho3 N3 O13 3+,3(Cl1 1-),H2 O1. From the CIF bond table, Ho01 (Ho) has 7 O neighbors; Ho02 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Ho03 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 3 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.496-3.562 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 95.70-99.42°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [{Ho3(OH)2(o-pbd)3Cl(H2O)5}2]·6Cl·2H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 5 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
